arenteral nutrition to help reduce infection rates during recovery. While bone marrow transplants have been performed in certain cases of ALD, the effectiveness of this treatment remains uncertain, particularly in advanced stages of the disease. However, it is considered a treatment option for patients who exhibit moderate neurological involvement in ALD.", "PACIENTES ASINTOMÁTICOS:Los pacientes asintomáticos pueden beneficiarse del tratamiento con aceite de Lorenzo, que reduce la frecuencia y severidad del deterioro neurológico.", "PACIENTES CON DISFUNCIÓN ADRENAL:Los pacientes con disfunción adrenal o neurológica preexistente pueden no ver mejoras con el tratamiento de aceite de Lorenzo.", "VALPROATO:Valproato is a medication that has shown neuroprotective capabilities in animal models for adrenoleucodistrofia and has potential antioxidant effects in patients.", "LOVASTATINA:Lovastatina, also known as lovastatin, is a medication primarily used to reduce cholesterol levels in the body. Its effectiveness can be influenced by food intake. Additionally, lovastatina has therapeutic applications beyond cholesterol management; it can also reduce AGCML levels in patients suffering from adrenoleucodistrofia. The drug functions by inhibiting nitric oxide synthase, contributing to its diverse pharmacological effects.", "BETA-INTERFERÓN:Beta-interferón is an immunosuppressive agent that has been tested for reducing inflammatory responses in brain lesions associated with ALD but has not shown significant clinical improvement.", "MITOXANTRONE:Mitoxantrone is an immunosuppressive agent that has been trialed for treating ALD-related brain lesions without significant success.", "INMUNOGLOBULINAS:Immunoglobulins, also known as \"inmunoglobulinas,\" are antibodies produced by the immune system that play a crucial role in identifying and neutralizing pathogens such as bacteria and viruses. They are essential components of the immune response and are found in bodily fluids like chyle. In addition to their protective functions, inmunoglobulinas have been investigated as immunosuppressive agents in the treatment of autoimmune liver disease (ALD) to help reduce inflammation. However, studies have indicated that they have not demonstrated significant clinical improvement in this context. Overall, inmunoglobulinas are vital for immune defense while also being explored for their potential therapeutic applications in certain medical conditions.", "BACLOFENO:Baclofeno is a medication used to treat spasticity as a complication of adrenoleucodistrofia.", "VIGABATRINA:Vigabatrina is a drug used to treat seizures in patients with adrenoleucodistrofia.", "FENOBARBITAL:Fenobarbital is a medication that enhances penetration into the nervous system and has a delayed elimination effect, which can lead to drowsiness. It is primarily used to control seizures in patients suffering from adrenoleucodystrophy.", "GENE X-ALD:Gene X-ALD is a gene related to adrenoleucodistrofia that is being researched for gene therapy applications.", "MITOCONDRIA:Mitochondria are cellular organelles where lipid β-oxidation occurs, crucial for energy production during fasting and stress.", "PEROXISOMAS:Peroxisomas are cellular organelles involved in lipid metabolism, particularly in the context of AGCML in adrenoleucodistrofia."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}